# f2 = run. `total` lies in the scope of make(). The turns read it for nothing but the sum that they store back, so it stays a number and is not held to int32 by a test a turn, and the counted loop
# takes its store as it takes the store of a module's variable: left out of the eight laid-out turns, made in front of each poll and where they hand over. It was 18.0 instructions a turn, a local's 3.5.
# RUN(NUMBER): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# NUMBER-LABEL: code f2:Body
# NUMBER: int|whole @Double) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# RUN(TURNS): emit f2 mechanisms=all
# TURNS-LABEL: unit f2:Body
# `i & 7` stands at two places of the text: nine of the one, among them the eight turns laid out, and one of the other. arm64 has one more BitAnd, at the entry, which is none of them.
# TURNS-COUNT-9: = BitAnd({{*}}origin = 101)
# TURNS-NOT: = BitAnd({{*}}origin = 101)
# RUN(OTHER): emit f2 mechanisms=all
# OTHER-COUNT-1: = BitAnd({{*}}origin = 70)
# OTHER-NOT: = BitAnd({{*}}origin = 70)
# RUN(EVENT): compile UnrolledLoopsEmitted UnrolledLoopStoresSunk UnrolledLoopIntegerSums mechanisms=all
# EVENT: statistic UnrolledLoopsEmitted 1
# EVENT: statistic UnrolledLoopStoresSunk 1
# EVENT: statistic UnrolledLoopIntegerSums 1
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell globalThis.count = () => 40;
# RIGHT: 140
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell globalThis.count = () => 0;
# NONE: 0
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
